===============================================================================
🌱 PHASE 1: FOUNDATION - BUILDING RECURSION INTUITION (Problems 1-10)
===============================================================================

Pattern: Basic Recursion Structure
Focus: Understanding base case, recursive case, and call stack

Problem 1: Print Numbers 1 to N ⭐
----------------------------------
Concept: Basic recursion with single parameter
Logic: Print current number, then recurse for n-1
Key Learning: Understanding call stack order

Problem 2: Print Numbers N to 1 ⭐
----------------------------------
Concept: Reverse order recursion
Logic: Recurse first, then print (post-order processing)
Key Learning: Order of operations in recursion

Problem 3: Calculate Factorial ⭐
---------------------------------
Concept: Mathematical recursion with return value
Logic: n! = n × (n-1)! with base case 0! = 1
Key Learning: Accumulating results through recursion

Problem 4: Calculate Sum 1 to N ⭐
---------------------------------
Concept: Accumulative recursion
Logic: sum(n) = n + sum(n-1) with base case sum(0) = 0
Key Learning: Building up results from smaller problems

Problem 5: Calculate Power (a^n) ⭐
----------------------------------
Concept: Two-parameter recursion
Logic: power(a,n) = a × power(a,n-1) with base case power(a,0) = 1
Key Learning: Multiple parameters in recursion

Problem 6: Fibonacci Sequence ⭐
-------------------------------
Concept: Classic recursion example
Logic: fib(n) = fib(n-1) + fib(n-2) with base cases fib(0)=0, fib(1)=1
Key Learning: Multiple base cases

Problem 7: Sum of Digits ⭐
--------------------------
Concept: Number processing recursion
Logic: Extract last digit, recurse with remaining digits
Key Learning: Processing number digit by digit

Problem 8: Count Digits ⭐
-------------------------
Concept: Counting through recursion
Logic: count(n) = 1 + count(n/10) with base case single digit
Key Learning: Using recursion for counting

Problem 9: Reverse a Number ⭐⭐
------------------------------
Concept: Helper function recursion
Logic: Use auxiliary parameter to build reverse
Key Learning: Helper functions with additional parameters

Problem 10: Check if Number is Palindrome ⭐⭐
--------------------------------------------
Concept: Combining multiple recursive operations
Logic: Compare number with its reverse using recursion
Key Learning: Composing recursive functions

===============================================================================
🔢 PHASE 2: LINEAR PROCESSING - SINGLE PATH RECURSION (Problems 11-20)
===============================================================================

Pattern: Single Recursive Call per Function
Focus: Array/String processing, linear data structures

Problem 11: Array Sum ⭐
-----------------------
Concept: Array traversal using recursion
Logic: sum(arr, n) = arr[n-1] + sum(arr, n-1)
Key Learning: Processing arrays recursively

Problem 12: Find Maximum in Array ⭐⭐
------------------------------------
Concept: Comparison-based recursion
Logic: max(arr, n) = Math.max(arr[n-1], max(arr, n-1))
Key Learning: Making decisions in recursion

Problem 13: Linear Search in Array ⭐⭐
--------------------------------------
Concept: Search pattern in recursion
Logic: Check current element, recurse for remaining
Key Learning: Early termination in recursion

Problem 14: Binary Search ⭐⭐
----------------------------
Concept: Divide and conquer introduction
Logic: Compare middle element, recurse on appropriate half
Key Learning: Reducing problem size by half

Problem 15: Check if String is Palindrome ⭐⭐
--------------------------------------------
Concept: Two-pointer recursion technique
Logic: Compare characters at both ends, recurse inward
Key Learning: Working with string indices

Problem 16: Reverse a String ⭐⭐
------------------------------
Concept: String processing with recursion
Logic: Take first character, append to reverse of rest
Key Learning: String manipulation in recursion

Problem 17: Count Vowels in String ⭐⭐
-------------------------------------
Concept: Conditional counting in recursion
Logic: Check current character, count if vowel, recurse
Key Learning: Conditional logic in recursive calls

Problem 18: Remove Character from String ⭐⭐
-------------------------------------------
Concept: String filtering with recursion
Logic: Skip target character, include others, recurse
Key Learning: Building filtered results

Problem 19: GCD of Two Numbers ⭐⭐
---------------------------------
Concept: Euclidean algorithm recursion
Logic: gcd(a,b) = gcd(b, a%b) with base case gcd(a,0) = a
Key Learning: Mathematical algorithms using recursion

Problem 20: Convert Decimal to Binary ⭐⭐
----------------------------------------
Concept: Number system conversion
Logic: Collect remainders while dividing by 2
Key Learning: Building results during recursion

===============================================================================
🌳 PHASE 3: TREE RECURSION - MULTIPLE PATH EXPLORATION (Problems 21-30)
===============================================================================

Pattern: Multiple Recursive Calls per Function
Focus: Decision trees, combinations, tree-like problems

Problem 21: Generate All Binary Strings of Length N ⭐⭐
------------------------------------------------------
Concept: Choice-based recursion (0 or 1 at each position)
Logic: For each position, try 0 and 1, recurse for remaining
Key Learning: Generating all possibilities

Problem 22: Print All Subsequences of String ⭐⭐⭐
-------------------------------------------------
Concept: Include/exclude pattern
Logic: For each character, generate subsequences with and without it
Key Learning: Exponential recursion patterns

Problem 23: Generate Power Set of Array ⭐⭐⭐
-------------------------------------------
Concept: Subset generation using recursion
Logic: For each element, include it or exclude it from current subset
Key Learning: Backtracking with collections

Problem 24: Count Ways to Climb Stairs ⭐⭐
-----------------------------------------
Concept: Dynamic programming with recursion
Logic: ways(n) = ways(n-1) + ways(n-2) (1 or 2 steps)
Key Learning: Overlapping subproblems

Problem 25: Coin Change Ways Count ⭐⭐⭐
-------------------------------------
Concept: Multiple choices at each step
Logic: For each coin, include it or exclude it
Key Learning: Optimization problems with recursion

Problem 26: Target Sum in Array ⭐⭐⭐
-----------------------------------
Concept: Subset sum problem
Logic: For each element, add to current sum or skip
Key Learning: Constraint satisfaction with recursion

Problem 27: Generate Balanced Parentheses ⭐⭐⭐
---------------------------------------------
Concept: Valid sequence generation
Logic: Add '(' if count < n, add ')' if close_count < open_count
Key Learning: Constraint-based generation

Problem 28: Tower of Hanoi ⭐⭐⭐
------------------------------
Concept: Classic divide and conquer
Logic: Move n-1 disks, move largest, move n-1 disks back
Key Learning: Complex problem decomposition

Problem 29: Josephus Problem ⭐⭐⭐
-------------------------------
Concept: Circular recursion pattern
Logic: J(n,k) = (J(n-1,k) + k) % n with base case J(1,k) = 0
Key Learning: Mathematical recursion relationships

Problem 30: Count Paths in Grid ⭐⭐⭐
-----------------------------------
Concept: Path counting with constraints
Logic: paths(i,j) = paths(i-1,j) + paths(i,j-1)
Key Learning: 2D recursion problems

